IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Defence Shelter Act 1997 (Singapore) -- which homes must have a shelter (ss 2, 3, 5), what owners and occupiers of
-- shelters must do and the penalties (ss 4, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12, 17, 18, 28(2)), when the emergency Parts switch on (s 1(3), (4)),
-- the Commissioner's emergency entry and cost recovery (s 10), entry on notice (s 15(3)), when a served notice is deemed received
-- (s 19(2), (3)), directors' liability (s 25) and composition (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CDSA1997.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the body is [15/2010] (s 23). The meta file records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0138 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short, so nearly all of it that touches an owner or occupier is here. Not encoded: s 2 definitions
-- beyond those the rules need, s 7 designation as a discretion, ss 13, 14 (administration and specifications), s 16 forcible
-- entry, ss 20 to 24 (inaccuracies, immunity, courts, prosecutions, evidence), s 27 exemption, the s 28 regulation-making powers
-- other than the s 28(2) cap, and the Schedule of MRT-station public shelters (s 2(3)). The regulations and the specifications
-- themselves were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Defence Shelter Act 1997 -- shelters`

§§ `2 and 3 -- which new homes must have a shelter`

-- s 2(1): "new house" and "new building" each mean a building "(a) which is constructed on vacant land or in place of a building
-- which has been demolished; and (b) the plans in respect of which are submitted to or lodged with the competent authority ...
-- on or after 1 May 1998". A "house" or "flat" is for private dwelling, "but does not include ... a hotel, hostel, dormitory or
-- nursing home or ... any other prescribed purposes".
-- s 3(1): "Every new house must be provided with a household shelter in accordance with the specifications."
-- s 3(2): every new building to be subdivided into flats must have (a) a household shelter in every flat, or (b) "in lieu of a
-- household shelter being provided in every flat on any storey ..., at least one storey shelter ... on that storey".
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `private dwelling`
    `hotel`
    `hostel`
    `dormitory`
    `nursing home`
    `non-residential use`

DECLARE Works IS ONE OF
    `built on vacant land`
    `built in place of a demolished building`
    `an extension or renovation of an existing building`

-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `the works` IS A Works, `plans lodged on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building is new dwelling stock under s 2` IF
        `the use` EQUALS `private dwelling`
    AND (`the works` EQUALS `built on vacant land` OR `the works` EQUALS `built in place of a demolished building`)
    AND `plans lodged on` AT LEAST 19980501

-- Per storey of a new building subdivided into flats (s 3(2)).
GIVEN `every flat on the storey has a household shelter` IS A BOOLEAN, `storey shelters on the storey` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the storey complies with s 3(2)` IF
    `every flat on the storey has a household shelter` OR `storey shelters on the storey` AT LEAST 1

§§ `5 -- public shelters in non-residential buildings`

-- s 5: "The Commissioner may require any statutory board to provide a public shelter ... in any new non-residential building
-- which is owned by the statutory board and the statutory board must comply". The Act imposes no like duty on a privately owned
-- non-residential building (that is a reading of s 5, not words of the Act).
GIVEN `owned by a statutory board` IS A BOOLEAN, `a new non-residential building` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Commissioner required it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a public shelter must be provided` IF
    `owned by a statutory board` AND `a new non-residential building` AND `the Commissioner required it`

§§ `4, 6, 8 -- the owner's or occupier's standing duties`

-- ss 4(1), 6(1), 8(1), in the same words for household and storey, public, and improvised shelters: the owner or occupier
-- "(c) must not carry out or permit another person to carry out therein, any repair or alteration, or anything else, which is
-- likely to damage or otherwise impair the efficient use of the ... shelter as such, except with the written permission of the
-- Commissioner ...; (d) must maintain the ... shelter in accordance with the regulations and such other directions as the
-- Commissioner may give ...; and (e) must carry out such works ... as the Commissioner may, from time to time, by writing require."
GIVEN `did something likely to impair the shelter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had the Commissioner's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `maintained it per the regulations and directions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `did the works required in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier is in breach of the shelter duties` IF
        (`did something likely to impair the shelter` AND (NOT `had the Commissioner's written permission`))
    OR  (NOT `maintained it per the regulations and directions`)
    OR  (NOT `did the works required in writing`)

DECLARE Shelter IS ONE OF
    `household shelter`
    `storey shelter`
    `public shelter`
    `improvised shelter`

-- s 7(2): an improvised shelter "ceases to be an improvised shelter when this Part ceases to be in operation, unless the
-- designation is sooner revoked".
GIVEN `Part 4 is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the designation was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the improvised shelter designation subsists` IF
    `Part 4 is in operation` AND (NOT `the designation was revoked`)

§§ `1(3), (4) -- when the emergency Parts 4 and 5 are in operation`

-- s 1(2): Parts 4 and 5 operate only as provided in (3) and (4). (3): the Minister may by order bring them into operation where a
-- Proclamation of Emergency or a declaration of a state of civil defence emergency "is imminent" and it is necessary for public
-- safety, for "such period as may be specified in the order". (4): the order "is not to be in force for a period exceeding 7 days
-- from the commencement of the order unless it has been made with the approval of the President".
GIVEN `days since the order commenced` IS A NUMBER, `days specified in the order` IS A NUMBER, `made with the President's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 1(3) order is in force` IF
        `days since the order commenced` AT MOST `days specified in the order`
    AND (`made with the President's approval` OR `days since the order commenced` AT MOST 7)

§§ `10, 11 -- shelters in an emergency`

-- s 10(1): where an owner or occupier of a part of a building "which consists of a storey shelter, a public shelter or an
-- improvised shelter" fails to comply with a s 9 notice in time, the Commissioner may enter, do the works "(including the seizure
-- and removal of any property)" and "(b) recover any costs and expenses ... from the owner or occupier". (2): "The Government
-- shall not be liable for any loss of or damage to any property seized or removed". A household shelter is not in the list.
GIVEN `the shelter` IS A Shelter, `a s 9 notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied within the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may enter, do the works and recover the costs` IF
        (NOT (`the shelter` EQUALS `household shelter`))
    AND `a s 9 notice was served`
    AND (NOT `complied within the time specified`)

-- s 11(1): the owner or occupier of a storey, public or improvised shelter "is bound, during the periods required or designated by
-- the Minister -- (a) to permit any person to enter and take refuge" and (b) to permit persons authorised by the Commissioner to
-- occupy or use it. (3): "It is a defence ... to prove ... that the person took all reasonable steps to ensure that all persons who
-- needed to enter and take refuge ... were allowed to do so."
GIVEN `the shelter` IS A Shelter, `in a period designated by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `someone was refused refuge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved all reasonable steps were taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing refuge is a s 11 offence` IF
        (NOT (`the shelter` EQUALS `household shelter`))
    AND `in a period designated by the Minister`
    AND `someone was refused refuge`
    AND (NOT `proved all reasonable steps were taken`)

§§ `12 -- using a shelter in peacetime`

-- s 12(1): the owner or occupier "may, at any time other than the period when an order made under section 1(3) is in operation,
-- use such part of the building for such purposes as may be -- (a) prescribed by the regulations; (b) approved by the Commissioner
-- in writing; or (c) allowed under any other written law." (2): "A person must not change the use ... without the prior written
-- approval of the Commissioner."
GIVEN `a s 1(3) order is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Commissioner approved the use in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another written law allows the use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the shelter is permitted` IF
        (NOT `a s 1(3) order is in operation`)
    AND (`the use is prescribed` OR `the Commissioner approved the use in writing` OR `another written law allows the use`)

§§ `15(3) -- entry to look for an improvised shelter`

-- s 15(3): the right of entry under (1)(a) (to see whether a building is suitable for an improvised shelter) is not to be exercised
-- "unless at least 24 hours' notice of the intended entry has been given". Entry under (1)(b) and (c) (shelters under construction,
-- existing shelters) carries no notice requirement in the text.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `to see if a building is suitable as an improvised shelter`
    `to inspect a shelter under construction`
    `to inspect an existing shelter`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 15 entry is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `to see if a building is suitable as an improvised shelter` THEN `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 24
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `19 -- when a served notice is deemed received`

-- s 19(3): personal delivery at the residence or workplace to an adult (1)(b) -- deemed conveyed "on the expiry of 6 hours from the
-- time of delivery"; registered post (1)(c) -- "48 hours from the time at which it was delivered to the post office"; affixing to
-- the building (1)(d) -- "24 hours"; broadcast or siren (2)(b), (c) -- "6 hours from the commencement of the first broadcast or
-- audible signal"; telephone to a family member or employee (2)(e) -- 6 hours; fax or telex (2)(f) -- 6 hours from first
-- transmission. Newspaper publication (2)(a) is deemed read "by noon on the day following the date of publication", which is not a
-- number of hours and is left out. Delivery to the person (1)(a) and telephone to the person (2)(d) carry no deeming rule; 0 here.
-- s 19(2): the methods in (2) are available only "during the period when an order made under section 1(3) is in operation".
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery to the person`
    `delivery to an adult at the residence or workplace`
    `registered post`
    `affixing to the building`
    `broadcast on radio and television`
    `siren or public-address signal`
    `reading it by telephone to the person`
    `reading it by telephone to a family member or employee`
    `fax or telex with acknowledgment`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Service
GIVETH A NUMBER
`hours until the notice is deemed received` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `delivery to an adult at the residence or workplace` THEN 6
    WHEN `registered post` THEN 48
    WHEN `affixing to the building` THEN 24
    WHEN `broadcast on radio and television` THEN 6
    WHEN `siren or public-address signal` THEN 6
    WHEN `reading it by telephone to a family member or employee` THEN 6
    WHEN `fax or telex with acknowledgment` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the method` IS A Service, `a s 1(3) order is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method of service is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `personal delivery to the person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `delivery to an adult at the residence or workplace` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registered post` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `affixing to the building` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `a s 1(3) order is in operation`

§§ `Penalties -- ss 4(2), 6(2), 8(2), 9(2), 11(2), 12(3), 17(2), 18, 28(2)`

-- s 4(2) household or storey shelter duties: fine to $5,000; continuing, a further $250 "for every day or part of a day ... after
--   conviction".
-- s 6(2) public shelter duties and s 8(2) improvised shelter duties: fine to $10,000 or imprisonment to 6 months or both;
--   continuing, $500 a day.
-- s 9(2) failing to prepare a shelter on notice; s 11(2) refusing refuge; s 12(3) use or change of use: fine to $10,000;
--   continuing, $500 a day; no imprisonment.
-- s 17(2) failing to furnish information, or furnishing false information: fine to $5,000; continuing, $250 a day.
-- s 18 obstructing the Commissioner or an authorised person: fine to $10,000 or imprisonment to 6 months or both; no daily fine.
-- s 28(2): regulations may make breaches punishable by a fine to $10,000 or imprisonment to 6 months or both (the cap).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 4 household or storey shelter duties`
    `s 6 public shelter duties`
    `s 8 improvised shelter duties`
    `s 9 failing to prepare a shelter on notice`
    `s 11 refusing refuge`
    `s 12 use or change of use`
    `s 17 information`
    `s 18 obstruction`
    `s 28 regulations cap`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 4 household or storey shelter duties` THEN 5000
    WHEN `s 17 information` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 6 public shelter duties` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 8 improvised shelter duties` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 18 obstruction` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 28 regulations cap` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine per day of continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 4 household or storey shelter duties` THEN 250
    WHEN `s 17 information` THEN 250
    WHEN `s 18 obstruction` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 28 regulations cap` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 500

-- Days (or parts of days) the offence continues after conviction, counted as whole days.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS `the further fine per day of continuing offence` `the offence` TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `25, 26 -- officers of companies, and composition`

-- s 25: where a body corporate, partnership or unincorporated association commits an offence, a director, manager, partner,
-- secretary or similar officer "shall be guilty of that offence unless the person proves that -- (a) the offence was committed
-- without his or her consent or connivance; and (b) the person had exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the
-- offence as he or she ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `the organisation committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty under s 25` IF
    `the organisation committed the offence` AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

-- s 26(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not
-- exceeding $500".
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum offered` AT MOST 500
